-- title:
--   Away-unit groups are commensurable with their conjugates
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the project predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is the whole algebra, and $R$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $r$ be a prime number, let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ with the image of $r$ lying in the prime ideal attached to $v$, and let $s$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Write $\tilde\Gamma$ for `CosetGraph.awayUnits R v`, the intersection over all height-one primes $w\neq v$ of the preimage, under the map $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b])^\times\to(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w)^\times$ induced by $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$, of the subgroup generated by those units $u$ of the completed algebra for which both $u$ and $u^{-1}$ lie in the local box [`Submodule.localBox R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40). The assertion is that the intersection $\tilde\Gamma\cap s\tilde\Gamma s^{-1}$, regarded as a subgroup of $\tilde\Gamma$, has finite index.
--
--   This is the commensurability of the unit group of an order in a quaternion algebra with its conjugates, in the "away from $v$" adelic form used to build the Čerednik–Drinfel'd coset graph; it is what makes the action of $\tilde\Gamma$ on that graph have finite vertex stabilisers and finitely many orbits. It is used in the proof that the even away-unit group, intersected with a level subgroup, has finitely many orbits on the relevant coset space.
-- source:
